 "structural_change": "COLLIO-SR2 10-23 (COORD tile review: split bodies 864 x 907, 6 small macros, ~2% fill, ~1.8k unregistered pins = BAD): ONE compact flat tile per face, top qfd_coll_face_p_fx = wires-only wrapper of the regional split face (qfd_coll_face_cx, RTL unchanged: L+2 as benched, lockstep + mutant witnesses results/rtl/cb16c_coll_1022/p_m*.log); the edge slices are the face pin registers on the root owning their band. Outline 518.4 x 388.8 from content; macros face the logic (u_rx R0 -> W rx band, bank0/u_tx MY -> spine, bank1-3 R0 -> spine); one bus per face (N tx_data, W rx_data, E phy); no 600-1200-um inter-entry hops left (largest tile span ~518 um). ALT: +21.6 spine / +10.8 channels (routing room). Band fences of the old body dropped (every root fits the compact outline).",
 "slot_change_request": "COLLIO-SR2 10-23: face tile shrinks from the 907.2-square face slot to 518.4 x 388.8 (one flat tile per face replaces body + 12 slices + wires-only parent); die lead re-slots the face",
